cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use or discuss this research foundation, please cite this repository
  and identify the specific version consulted. A DOI may be added after a
  corresponding archived release is registered.
type: software
title: 'Adversarial Structural Security Intelligence (ASSI): Research Foundation'
abstract: >-
  ASSI is a specification-first research framework investigating structural
  security beyond cryptographic validity. It develops research proposals for
  compositional identity and UTN, directional weak evidence and REN,
  bidirectional conditional evidence feedback (BCEF), independently governed
  authorization, adversarial security drives, security residuals, autonomous
  questioning, and validated recursive self-improvement. The v0.1.0 release
  is a research foundation, not an implementation, security certification,
  or claim of empirical validation.
